  "mechanismNote": "gown vertices inside the body skin are measured and bodice-concentrated: +X-ray even-odd 395 upper vs 31 lower, +Z-ray 705 vs 153, nearest-surface 506 vs 0. The gather band (automate_blender.py #686: _fold_amp686=0.034m triangle-wave on a 10-22mm conformal offset) puts the wave valleys 12-24mm inside the body surface across y 0.98..1.51 (body f 0.55..0.86), fading at both band edges — which is where the shards are densest and where they fade. Degenerate triangles are negligible (483 below 1e-8 m^2, 81 below 1e-12) and sit near the collar, not the placket. Inward-facing normals (axis reference) are upper-heavy but dominated by correct inner-sleeve tube surfaces and accordion flank normals near dot~0; the nearest-surface reference is biased at free rims. Neither is the discriminator the interpenetration is."
